\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: European Summary\b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2011\par 14:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Energy Service\par \uc2 NRG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1310 GMT (Dow Jones) EUROPEAN SUMMARY: A \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate hike and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Egyptian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were the highlights of an otherwise uninspiring session. USD weakness seen in Asia fed through into Europe although it was not one-way traffic. Mid-session China hiked all rates by 25bp, which caught the market on the hop coming one day before Chinese markets reopen from the Lunar holiday. The risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately dipped on the move and while most quickly rebounded AUD continued to suffer due to the many trade links between the two countries. Meanwhile German December industrial production sank 1.5% against a 0.3% decline expected but again had minimal impact on the euro. Sterling had a rare underperforming session; early support from strong overnight RICS housing survey and BRC retail sales faded, with news the UK government has made the bank levy on profits permanent cited as one reason for the pound's slippage.\par \par \uc2  GBP/USD currently at the day's low of 1.6084 from 1.6161, EUR/USD traded 1.3593-1.3667, USD/JPY a no-show between 81.99-82.21 while AUD/USD slipped to 1.0114 from 1.0192. Elsewhere, the Bank of Greece \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rapid fall in the Egyptian pound seen since domestic banks reopened Monday. USD/EGP collapsed to 5.8751 after printing a fresh 10-year high of 5.9651 Tuesday. EUR/SEK printed yet another 10-year low of 8.7643. Away from the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets core European government bonds trade flat although lower demand at the ECB's weekly and monthly cash tenders pushed short-term German yields higher. March bunds are currently -0.01 at 122.85, March gilts +0.02 at 115.85. The main European equity bourses trade 0.1% around par after taking a small dip on China's rate hike. Oil's $1.50 drop to a one-week low of $85.95 is all related to China while gold is a down 60c at $1350oz. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London: +44-20-7842-9464; markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 02-08-11 0810ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1085 75112 8764   \par \par \uc2 Dokument NRG0000020110208e7280001l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
