\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Former PBOC Adviser:China Aims To Keep GDP Growth Slightly Lower Than 8%--Report\b0\par\par\uc2 233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2011\par 02:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 29 Jan 2011 20:26 EDT *DJ  Former PBOC Adviser: Hope To Keep Such GDP Growth In 10 Years--Report\par \par \uc2 29 Jan 2011 20:33 EDT *DJ  Former PBOC Adviser: \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Should Stop \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 --Report\par \par \uc2 29 Jan 2011 20:33 EDT *DJ  Former PBOC Adviser: China Should Let Yuan Rise Naturally--Report\par \par \uc2 29 Jan 2011 20:40 EDT DJ  Former PBOC Adviser:China Aims To Keep GDP Growth Slightly Lower Than 8%--Report\par \par \uc2 BEIJING (Dow Jones)--China intends to keep its annual gross domestic product growth rate slightly below 8% for the next five years, a former Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adviser was quoted as saying over the weekend by Chinese news website Sina.com.\par \par \uc2 China hopes to maintain such a growth rate for 10 years, Yu Yongding, an economist from the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences, a major government think tank, was cited as saying in the report.\par \par \uc2 China should also stop acquiring U.S. government debt and halt its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, thus allowing the yuan to rise naturally, Yu said in the report, adding that this was only his personal view.\par \par \uc2 -By Aaron Back and Liu Li, Dow Jones Newswires; (8610) 8400-7701; aaron.back@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 29, 2011 20:40 ET (01:40 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110130e71u0002w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pic