\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2011\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S EXPORTS TO CHINA AT RECORD HIGH IN 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's exports to China hit a record high in 2010 due mainly to demand for autos and machinery, underscoring the importance of China's growth to the export-dependent Japanese economy as overall shipments showed signs of recovery in December. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: KOREA CURRENT-ACCOUNT SURPLUS RISES; TO EASE IN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's current-account surplus rose in December as the nation exported more automobiles, ships and electronics, bringing the surplus for the full year to the fourth-largest on record and providing further support to the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TRICHET: COULD BE USEFUL FOR EFSF TO BUY GOVERNMENT BONDS - BLOOMBERG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said governments could empower the European Financial Stability Facility, the region's bailout fund, to buy bonds, a move that would take pressure off the ECB's efforts to fight the sovereign-debt crisis, Bloomberg News reported. (published 0110 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: RBNZ LEAVES OCR UNCHANGED AT 3.00% ON WEAK ACTIVITY, LACK OF INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand Thursday held the Official Cash Rate at 3.00% given weak domestic economic activity and a lack of inflationary pressures. (published 2124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC VICE GOV MA: TO ADJUST VARIABLE RESERVE REQUIREMENTS IN MORE TRANSPARENT, REGULATED WAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will adjust differentiated reserve requirements ratios for banks in a more transparent and regulated way in 2011, as part of its efforts to curb liquidity and inflation, bank Vice Gov. Ma Delun said in a statement dated Wednesday. (published 0102 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA UNVEILS A$1.8B TAX TO FUND FLOOD CLEANUP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Prime Minister Julia Gillard staked the popularity of her minority administration Thursday on a new A$1.8 billion tax to help fund reconstruction in flood-devastated Queensland state without tipping the government budget further into deficit. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN ECONOMIC VITAL SIGNS SLOWED BEFORE FLOODS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economic vital signs were already slowing in November, before the rains and flooding that devastated large parts of Queensland state in December and January. (published 0014 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN EX-MOF UTSUMI: DOLLAR MAY RISE TO Y85-Y90 RANGE BY JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese yen may weaken to a range of Y85-Y90 versus the dollar and to a Y115-Y125 band versus the euro by the end of June due to expected declines in demand for the safe-haven asset, said a former top Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official who guided the country through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaigns in the past. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THINK TANK: SEE 1ST-QUARTER GDP UP 9%, CPI UP 5% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The State Information Center expects China's gross domestic product to grow around 9% in the first quarter and the consumer price index to rise about 5%, according to a report from the government think tank published in the China Securities Journal on Thursday. (published 0004 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM JANUARY TRADE DEFICIT NARROWS TO $1.0 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's trade deficit narrowed to $1 billion in January from a revised $1.294 billion a month earlier, the government said, as imports of products such as chemicals, fabric, steel and automobiles declined. (published 0245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PEMBINAAN BLT SEEKS TO RAISE MYR1 BLN VIA 6 TRANCHES OF SUKUK - DOCUMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pembinaan BLT Sdn Bhd, a wholly-owned construction company of the Malaysian government, is seeking raise MYR1 billion via six tranches of Islamic bonds, or sukuk, with an option to upsize the offering, according to a document obtained by Dow Jones Newswires Thursday. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 27-01-11 0400GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110127e71r0008c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
