\par\par \b \uc2 Taiwan dlr sinks on c.bank move, euro;  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  in focus\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2010\par 02:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  * Suspected c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushes Taiwan dollar lower\par \par \uc2  * Euro, world stock mkts fall over issues in Ireland, China  (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, Nov 17 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> eased on Wednesday on susp-ected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following downward pressure from a sinking euro, the prospect of tightening in China, and year-end investor risk aversion.\par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at T$30.793 per U.S. dollar, compared with its Tuesday close of T$30.732, largely due to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move to offset earlier gains.\par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar has gained about 3 percent since late September in anticipation of U.S. monetary easing that became a reality earlier this month.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to control volatility and protect the island's export competitiveness, and some investors are bracing for possible stronger measures.\par \par \uc2  Also on Wednesday, the Taiwan dollar joined other emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in losing ground to a drop in the euro over Irish debt [ID:nLDE6AG004] and to expectations of tighter credit in China. [ID:nTOE6AG02L]\par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like other high-risk assets, is not expected to see major gains until 2011 as investors take profit and steer clear of risk until year-end, strategists say.\par \par \uc2  "People can take a bit of a breather," said Charles Han, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 Newedge Group\uc2  in Hong Kong. "You're going to see more risk-aversion trades into year end."\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       0800 GMT        PREVIOUS SESSION CLOSE\par T$ (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Taipei \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 )      30.793                    30.732\par  T$ (Cosmos1)           30.445                    30.250\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taipei \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  is Taiwan's main \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange; Cosmos is a\par small exchange.\par NDFs (vs U.S. dollar)\par                0836 GMT            PREVIOUS SESSION, 0802 GMT\par  6-month       T$30.120                      T$29.835\par  2-year        T$29.150                      T$29.161\par Net foreign trading in Taiwan stocks (T$ bln)\par   Wednesday              Month to date               October\par     -11.319                  54.292                   40.372\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (See [EMRG/FRX] for a table of year-to-date Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par performance.)\par  (Reporting by Ralph Jennings; Editing by Chris Lewis)\par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 -TAIWAN/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|Z|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101120e6bh00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
