\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2010\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN SEES G-20 LEADERS AGREEING ON NEED FOR CURR ACCT GUIDELINES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Tuesday that the leaders of the Group of 20 industrial and developing countries may agree on the need for "indicative guidelines" to mend global trade imbalances, but they probably won't settle the specific details, and instead, will leave that to the finance ministers. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA FINANCE MINISTER: SOME MAJOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ISSUERS HAVE OVERLY LOOSE MONETARY POLICY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Finance Minister Xie Xuren said Tuesday that some issuers of major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have had excessively loose monetary policies, an apparent reference to the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy of quantitative easing that has prompted a series of complaints from Chinese officials. (published 0122 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA VICE PREMIER: FINANCIAL VOLATILITY AFFECTING MARKET CONFIDENCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Vice Premier Wang Qishan said Tuesday he sees excessive global liquidity, adding that volatility in international financial markets is affecting market confidence. (published 0146 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OECD: MAJOR ASEAN ECONOMIES RETURNING TO PRE-CRISIS GROWTH RATES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The six major economies of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations are seeing strong growth and should be able to post 2011-15 annual GDP expansion of 6.0% on average, equal to what they saw before the 2008 global financial crisis, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said in a report Tuesday. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN SEPT UNADJUSTED CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS RISES 24.3% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's current account surplus expanded in September as imports increased at a slower pace, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA VOWS A$3.45B SPENDING CUTS TO KEEP SURPLUS PROMISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian government Tuesday reaffirmed its pledge to restore the budget to surplus in the fiscal year starting July 1, 2012, underpinned by spending cuts of A$3.45 billion to offset the corrosive impact on government revenues of an Australian dollar trading at post-float highs. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN BUSINESS CONFIDENCE FALLS 2 PTS TO +8 IN OCT VS SEPT - NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business confidence fell for a second straight month in October, hurt by the prospect of rising interest rates and a surging Australian dollar's impact on exporters. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN, US TO LAUNCH DIALOGUE TO SECURE RARE EARTH MINERALS - KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo and Washington have decided to launch high-level talks on resources and energy in a bid to secure rare earth minerals amid stalled exports of them from China, Kyodo News reported Tuesday citing sources close to Japan-U.S. relations. (published 0136 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA TO INVEST $6.6B IN INDONESIAN INFRASTRUCTURE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has pledged to invest $6.6 billion in infrastructure projects in Indonesia, the Jakarta Globe reported Tuesday. (published 0104 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO ALLOW LOCAL GOVERNMENTS TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN PROPERTY SECTOR - REPORT \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is planning measures that will allow local governments to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the property market to prevent fast increases in property prices, the state-run Securities Times reported Tuesday, citing unnamed sources. (published 0043 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RATE HIKES POSE BIGGEST RISK TO CHINA MORTGAGE LOANS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Any further interest-rate hikes in China would be the biggest risk for domestic mortgage loans totaling trillions of yuan, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Tuesday, citing a government think tank. (published 0114 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF: CHINA SELLS NET Y769.2B JAPAN FINANCIAL ASSETS IN SEP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's sales of Japanese financial assets including government bonds declined in September, data from Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed Tuesday. (published 0126 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OVERSEA-CHINESE BANKING PRICES US$500 MLN TIER 2 SUBORDINATED NOTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday said it has priced US$500 million of subordinated notes at 99.367% and expects to issue the notes on Nov. 15. (published 2341 GMT) [ 09-11-10 0200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101109e6b90005m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
