\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dollar dips; consolidation before Bernanke\b0\par\par\uc2 843 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2010\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Sing dollar dips on US dollar short-covering\par \par \uc2 * Eyes on Bernanke, U.S. report on \b \highlight22\uc2 China FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Thailand spotted\par \par \uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar edged down against the dollar on Friday as investors covered dollar-short positions and dealers spotted Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overall showed some consolidation with the South Korean won erasing most of its earlier losses before a speech by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke later in the day.\par \par \uc2 Bernanke's comments are unlikely to change expectations of further easing by the Fed to help fuel the world's top economy, which have helped lift Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It is not a time for Bernanke to give another signal. He will confirm the Fed's existing stance, which will continue to support Asia," said Kim Jae-eun, an economist at \uc2 Hyundai Securities\uc2  in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> rose, recovering from suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Market players are also keeping an eye on the U.S. Treasury Department's comments on China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices later in the day. Before the report, spot yuan <CNY=CFXS> hit its highest the dollar since its landmark revaluation in July 2005. [ID:nTOE69E01X]\par \par \uc2 But dealers trading on the Chinese market see little chance of Washington labelling China a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.\par \par \uc2 Regional authorities were estimated to have bought a combined $33.8 billion via \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Sept 27 and Oct 13, according to traders' estimates compiled by IFR Markets. [ID:nSGE69D0EW]\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> <SGD=D3> fell slightly against the U.S. dollar as investors covered U.S. dollar-short positions in thin trading before the weekend.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record high after the country widened the trading band for the first time since just after the 9/11 attacks on the United States, underlining the depth of its concern about financial markets. [ID:nSGE69B08J]\par \par \uc2 "Those who oversold the dollar yesterday are buying back today to square (positions) for the weekend. But the market is overall quiet as we go between 1.2960 and 1.2990 today," said a Singapore-based dealer.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The baht <THB=TH> was steady with a slightly softer tone in early trade while its Asian peers eased on profit-taking after recent heady gains.\par \par \uc2 "The baht is being confined to a narrow 29.83-85 range by light \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer at a Thai bank said. "The market is waiting to see whether the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  will do anything to check capital inflows. For the policy rate review next Wednesday, the growing noise from the business sector against a rate hike means it is now 50:50 on whether the BOT will raise rates or hold [ID:nSGE69D0BQ]."\par \par \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, Prasarn Trairatvorakul, said on Friday the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  would exercise caution in adopting any additional measures in dealing with the baht's fast appreciation to avoid market disruption [ID:nTST000119].\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won erased most of its earlier losses to end flat against the dollar as exporters chased it for settlements, prompting investors to clear dollar-long positions.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as market players covered dollar-short positions amid a broad rebound in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on caution over Seoul's possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The won is seen rising very slowly. The U.S. quantitative theme will keep supporting it, but everybody is cautious around 1,110," said a Seoul-based local bank dealer.\par \par \uc2 Some dealers suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities of buying dollars to check the won's strength. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0725 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        81.23          81.44       +0.26\par  Sing dlr        1.2960         1.2947       -0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      30.640         30.770       +0.42\par  Korean won     1111.00        1110.90       -0.01\par  Baht             29.80          29.79       -0.03\par  Peso             43.19          43.17       -0.05\par  Rupiah         8920.00        8920.00       +0.00\par  Rupee            44.08          44.10       +0.05\par  Ringgit         3.0830         3.0820       -0.03\par  Yuan            6.6429         6.6508       +0.12\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        81.23          92.90      +14.37\par  Sing dlr        1.2960         1.4053       +8.43\par  Taiwan dlr      30.640         32.030       +4.54\par  Korean won     1111.00        1164.50       +4.82\par  Bah