upgrades to Buy vs Underperform on higher product margins; Nan Ya (1303.TW) also +4.4% at NT$66.70. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0604 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR extends losses, touches fresh intraday low of 44.09 on heavy selling pressure ahead of \uc2 Coal India Ltd\uc2 's share sale Monday, says trader with state-run bank. Pair now at 44.20 vs 44.52 late Wednesday. "Inflows are particularly heavy today, largely driven by foreign funds' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversion into rupees. The pair may touch the 44.00 level if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , something that is being keenly watched at these levels," trader says. Adds, oil importers had been sitting on sidelines but 44.10 provided good level for buying. Tips pair in 44.00-44.30 band for session. (khushita.vasant@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0546 GMT [Dow Jones] Bank of Korea likely to raise rates by 25 bps by year-end, given BOK's fairly positive economic assessment, inflation risks stemming from higher commodity prices, rising domestic demand, according to \uc2 HSBC\uc2  economist Song-yi Kim; notes, "it is clear enough that the BOK's decision to keep its policy rate unchanged today is dominated by its concern about Korea's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...but we believe that there is still some chance that the BOK will have to move on rates before the year-end...the MPC still remains biased toward further tightening." Adds, domestic consumption looks to remain supportive of overall economic growth, with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength likely to boost consumption, through better purchasing power. BOK earlier today kept policy rate unchanged at 2.25% for third straight month. (In-Soo.Nam@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0543 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares +0.5% at 997.94 at midday break, flirting yet again with 1000 point level, in active trade as PTT (PT