\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:Thai Shares +0.5% At Midday;1000 Resistance Tipped\b0\par\par\uc2 1,725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 07:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0543 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares +0.5% at 997.94 at midday break, flirting yet again with 1000 point level, in active trade as PTT (PTT.TH) group shares push higher on rising oil prices, while banking sector also bubbling along ahead of expected robust 3Q earnings. "I think the SET Index should test 1000 today for sure, but I don't think it can stay above 1000 today as it's a key resistance level for investors," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kim Eng Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Mayuree Chowvikran. Resistance at 1000, support at 995. Among top actives, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PTT Aromatics and Refining\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PTTAR.TH) +3.5% at THB29.50, PTT (PTT.TH) +1.0% at THB312, \f28 \uc2 \f2 PTT Exploration and Production\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PTTEP.TH) +1.2% at THB174, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Krung Thai Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  (KTB.TH) +1.7% at THB17.70, Bangkok Bank (BBL.TH) +0.9% at THB161.50. (leigh.murray@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0538 GMT [Dow Jones] KRW IRS down sharply as BOK's decision to keep key policy rate on hold at 2.25% for 3rd straight month fan view \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely to resume tightening until next year, participants say; 2-year IRS down sharply at 3.180% vs 3.272% late yesterday, 5-year down at 3.540% vs 3.618%, December bond futures +48 ticks at 113.23. Yield curve steepening slightly and "I think bonds could strengthen a bit more from here given that people are thinking no rate hike will be in the pipeline for the rest of this year," though there's not much room for yields to fall today, says swap broker with foreign brokerage. Says