t Russell 3000 Index, note says; adds, throughout period, Russell 3000 reflected average 2-year correlation of 0.50 with Russell India Index and 0.48 with Russell China Index. "While the Russell China Index has correlated to the U.S. market at a relatively steady degree during the 14-year period from September of 1996 through September of 2010, staying within a range of 0.30 and 0.75, India's correlation to the Russell 3000 has increased more so since 2006, reaching a 0.80 correlation point in 2009." (john.kumar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0516 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares by midday +0.5% at 3628.477 in moderate volume, off earlier high of 3643.771, led by foreign-buying in most blue chips amid hopes for strong 9-month earnings, traders say; tip resistance at 3650. "Overall sentiment however, looks cautious as local institutional funds continue to take profit," says trader at Lautandhana Securities . Foreigners net buyers of IDR180 billion worth of shares. Among gainers; gas distributor Gas Negara (PGAS.JK) +3.1% at IDR4,125, coal miner Adaro (ADRO.JK) +4.8% at IDR2,200, while Bank Negara (BBNI.JK) also +2.5% at IDR4,100. Profit-taking hits \uc2 XL Axiata\uc2  (EXCL.JK) down 4.3% at IDR5,550. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0457 GMT [Dow Jones] As many other developed economies consider further easing of monetary policy, Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands alone in contemplating further rate rises, says Heard on the Street; since RBA left rates on hold last week, surprising many, strong consumer sentiment and jobs data has made a hike next month seem a certainty. But AUD approaching parity with USD, a worry for Australia's exporting industries; already there's talk success of the country's mining sector, on the back of Chinese growth, is causing "Dutch disease" -- the concern being that success of resources industry could dampen prospects for rest of economy. See: HEARD ON THE STREET: Australia's Lonely \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (andrew.peaple@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0446 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares end +0.2% at 458.66 as foreigners extend their recent buying-streak amid growing optimism more banks will lower lending rates, while government continues to help companies lower \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  costs. "Market sentiment will improve because more banks are expected to cut their lending rates. Also, foreigners are buying these days so we expect more gains tomorrow," says Eurocapital Securities analyst. Volume thin with 23.3 million shares valued at VND597 billion traded. Among actives, Meco (MCG.VH) ends +4.7% at VND17,900, \uc2 PetroVietnam\uc2  Fertilizer (DPM.VH) ends +1.8% at VND33,500, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) ends down 0.3% at VND30,000. Tips key index to move in 460-465 Friday. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0444 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia shares turn flat after breaching psychological 1,500 level; profit-taking in blue-chips erase early gains; KLCI up 0.35 points at 1,497.32 midday. Dealer says short term positive trend intact, but adds 1,500 to act as strong barrier with profit-taking likely to limit gains at any rally; tips 1,495-1,505 range for rest of session. Investors continue to favor construction stocks on hopes of positive newsflow from 2011 budget tomorrow; sub-index +0.7%; Market breadth slightly positive with 363 gainers vs 334 decliners; gainers include plantation stocks \uc2 KL Kepong\uc2  (2445.KU) +3.9% at MYR19.32, \uc2 IOI Corp\uc2 . (1961.KU) +1.0% at MYR5.80; \uc2 MMC Corp\uc2 . (2194.KU) +1.3% at MYR3.10; Manulife (1058.KU) +12% at MYR3.18 after major shareholder makes offer to buy out rest of shares in insurer; among decliners \uc2 GuocoLand\uc2  (1503.KU) down 5.0% at MYR1.15, MK Land (8893.KU) down 2.8% at MYR0.345, both after yesterday's gains.(ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0440 GMT [Dow Jones] AUD/USD parity seems inevitable, but concerns growing a pullback could be in cards if central banks don't do what market expects them to, says Sydney-based \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist. "Fundamentally, there is little standing in the way and it's pretty much at parity already. But there remains this possibility the RBA won't go (to higher rates) in November on the threat of commercial banks raising lending rates. And the FOMC could decide to implement other measures before they buy Treasury securities outright," says the strategist. AUD/USD recently at 0.9960, just off new post-float high of 0.9982 hit in early afternoon trading. (geoffrey.rogow@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0440 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore shares pare gains as investors take some money off table with prices at 29-month highs. Market breadth flat vs 5 gainers for every decliner in early trade. STI +0.1% at 3206.83 midday vs 3220.51 morning high (new year-to-date intraday peak, highest since May 2008), which could provide resistance for rest of day. "The market has come off a bit, with some mixed reaction to the MAS tightening. But a pullback shouldn't be surprising as we had a good run yesterday," says local house trader. Wilmar (F34.SG) top percentage gainer among blue chips, +4.1% at S$6.40, on hopes plantation group will benefit from higher cooking oil prices in China. \uc2 Keppel Corp\uc2 . (BN4.SG) down 0.7% at S$9.78, SembMarine (S51.SG) off 0.2% at S$4.40; stronger SGD vs USD deemed tad negative for rig builders as bulk of their contracts denominated in USD. Overall volume modest at 1.19 billion shares worth S$1.17 billion. (frankie.ho@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0437 GMT [Dow Jones] After downbeat production report from its 75%-owned \uc2 Coal & Allied\uc2  (CNA.AU) yesterday, \uc2 UBS\uc2  expected production declines and guidance downgrades for \uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2 's (RIO.AU) coal production. Thermal coal FY10 guidance came in worse than \uc2 UBS\uc2  estimate, 19.1 million tons vs 19.7 million tons; but most valuable hard coking coal was guided at 9.5 million tons in FY10 vs 9.4 million tons estimate, while 2.4 million tons mined in 3Q came in well above 2.2 million tons estimate. Copper more downbeat, coming in at 159,000 tons mined vs 169,900 estimate. (david.fickling@dowjones.com) [ 10-14-10 0138ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101014e6ae0004a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
