at 3206.83 midday vs 3220.51 morning high (new year-to-date intraday peak, highest since May 2008), which could provide resistance for rest of day. "The market has come off a bit, with some mixed reaction to the MAS tightening. But a pullback shouldn't be surprising as we had a good run yesterday," says local house trader. Wilmar (F34.SG) top percentage gainer among blue chips, +4.1% at S$6.40, on hopes plantation group will benefit from higher cooking oil prices in China. \uc2 Keppel Corp\uc2 . (BN4.SG) down 0.7% at S$9.78, SembMarine (S51.SG) off 0.2% at S$4.40; stronger SGD vs USD deemed tad negative for rig builders as bulk of their contracts denominated in USD. Overall volume modest at 1.19 billion shares worth S$1.17 billion. (frankie.ho@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0437 GMT [Dow Jones] After downbeat production report from its 75%-owned \uc2 Coal & Allied\uc2  (CNA.AU) yesterday, \uc2 UBS\uc2  expected production declines and guidance downgrades for \uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2 's (RIO.AU) coal production. Thermal coal FY10 guidance came in worse than \uc2 UBS\uc2  estimate, 19.1 million tons vs 19.7 million tons; but most valuable hard coking coal was guided at 9.5 million tons in FY10 vs 9.4 million tons estimate, while 2.4 million tons mined in 3Q came in well above 2.2 million tons estimate. Copper more downbeat, coming in at 159,000 tons mined vs 169,900 estimate. (david.fickling@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0436 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by 1-month ATM USD/JPY options down tad at 11.60%/12.30% from 11.65%/12.35% Wednesday in New York as stability in spot early in morning in global day prompted some players to trim USD downside hedges, says options dealer at major Japan bank. But sharp falls in vols unlikely for rest of global day as some demand for USD downside hedges later returns after USD/JPY marks fresh 15-year low at 81.23 in late Tokyo morning trade. Such demand may be sustained ahead amid view Japan PM Kan's comments Wednesday that G-20 countries,