\par\par \b \uc2 TAKE-A-LOOK- \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  stand-off entrenched ahead of G20\b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 15:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 G20 nations are under pressure to resolve disputes about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy or risk a new crisis for the world economy as protectionism takes hold.\par \par \uc2 After a weekend IMF meeting failed to make any headway, Thailand slapped a tax on foreign investment in government debt on Tuesday in a bid to brake the baht, Japan said it would wade into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market anew if need be to weaken the yen, and Beijing once again talked down the prospects of a faster rise in the yuan.\par \par \uc2 G20 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors meet in South Korea from Oct. 22 with a leaders summit convening on Nov. 11.\par \par \uc2 Double-click on codes in brackets for stories about the key issues at the meetings. For a diary on the meetings, see [IMF/DIARY]. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ------------------------------------------------------------------------\par         For a PDF report "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Race to the bottom"\par                 \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/gez77p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/gez77p}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  ------------------------------------------------------------------------\par  MAIN STORY\par > Asia stiffens resolve to resist capital inflows         [ID:nTOE69B03A]\par  \par  OTHER LATEST STORIES\par > Thailand sets bond tax to curb inflows, tame baht       [ID:nSGE69B0A6]\par > Japan's Noda vows decisive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves after G7 meeting    [ID:nTOE69B00D]\par > China says \f28 \b \highligh