\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. set to be a posse of one on China yuan at G20\b0\par\par\uc2 914 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2010\par 18:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Geithner may stand alone on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue\par \par \uc2 * G20 host South Korea says yuan inappropriate topic\par \par \uc2 * U.S. administration tries to placate Congress\par \par \uc2 * China's economic clout silences critics\par \par \uc2 By Paul Eckert\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Sept 26 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner faces a lonely campaign to make China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a major issue at the next Group of 20 summit as would-be allies shrink from confronting Beijing.\par \par \uc2 Pressured by U.S. lawmakers, Geithner vowed last week to mobilize countries at the Nov. 11-12 summit in South Korea to press China for faster appreciation of the yuan <CNY=CFXS>.\par \par \uc2 Interviews with officials from G20 countries suggest that Geithner -- who has acknowledged that few countries are willing to confront China -- could be leading a posse of one in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. is more determined than the rest of the G20 to get something out of China on the yuan," a euro zone monetary official said, speaking on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 "It's largely a bilateral matter with the rest looking on as spectators, either because they don't count enough or because they aren't very interested," the official said.\par \par \uc2 South Korean Finance Minister Yoon Jeung-hyun ruled out the yuan as a G20 topic, saying the forum might take up exchange rates in general or their impact on the global economy.\par \par \uc2 "But aside from that, I do not believe that it is appropriate to have a discussion regarding the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate or level of a specific country," Yoon said in an interview with Reuters in Paris on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Geithner's drive to make China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy a G20 summit issue appears to be a way to buy time for President Barack Obama's administration as it deals with an angry Congress in the run-up to Nov. 2 U.S. elections.\par \par \uc2 The Obama administration, and Geithner in particular, had largely avoided actions that would antagonize China in past G20 meetings. But it faces an increasing drumbeat of calls for action on the yuan from beleaguered Democrats who say a stronger Chinese yuan would bring relief to American workers.\par \par \uc2 In a move likely to increase tension with China, the House of Representatives Ways and Means Committee on Friday approved a bill that would let the United States slap duties on goods from countries with undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bill may never become law, however, because it faces uncertain prospects in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Since China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June said it would let the yuan <CNY=CFXS> fluctuate more freely, it has risen 1.8 percent -- accelerating the most as U.S. pressure mounted.\par \par \uc2 Many U.S. lawmakers believe that China keeps its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  undervalued by as much as 40 percent to stoke exports at the expense of U.S. jobs, a claim questioned by many economists.\par \par \uc2 BRIC SOLIDARITY, ASIAN DEPENDENCY\par \par \uc2 China can count on solidarity from its partners in the so-called BRIC countries -- Brazil, Russia and India.\par \par \uc2 "I believe that this idea of putting pressure on a country is not the right way for finding solutions," Brazilian Foreign Minister Celso Amorim told Reuters last week.\par \par \uc2 Brazil, he said, enjoyed good coordination with China and "we can't forget that China is currently our main customer."\par \par \uc2 Russia likewise enjoys its trading relationship with China, exporting raw materials and energy but not the manufactured goods that compete against low-cost Chinese goods. Moscow tends to speak only in general terms about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.\par \par \uc2 "Russia is unlikely to back this," said Evgeny Gavrilenkov, chief economist at Troika Dialog in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 "Russia does not have a big trade relationship with China, and politically I do not think it is profitable for Russia to back this either," he said.\par \par \uc2 Visiting New York this past week for the U.N. General Assembly, Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao flatly rejected any link between the level of the Chinese yuan and U.S. trade deficits.\par \par \uc2 China is increasingly assertive as its economic power grows -- all the more so in neighboring Asia.\par \par \uc2 It is home to five other G20 members, most of whom count China as their biggest trade partner.\par \par \uc2 "The rise of China, the increasing prominence of China, is a fact of life," said Indonesian Foreign Minister Marty Natalegawa.\par \par \uc2 "It is something that we must all embrace, and celebrate as a matter of fact, because Indonesia is benefiting as well with \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's increasing economic prominence," he said.\par \par \uc2 Japan's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down from 15-year highs against the dollar makes Tokyo an unlikely standard-bearer for exchange rate rectitude and an awkward partner for any U.S. pressure on China, say analysts.\par \par \uc2 A second European monetary official predicted talk, but no walk at the G20 meetings.\par \par \uc2 "It's obvious that we talk about it, but that's as far as it goes. It's not on the agenda of Korea's G20 presidency and it wont be a major issue," said the official.\par \par \uc2 "China has basically been pretending to take significant steps on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a long time, and I don't expect that to change for the time being," he added. (Additional reporting by Toni Vorobyova in Moscow, Walter Brandimarte in New York, Doug Palmer in Washington and Daniel Flynn in Paris; Editing by Maureen Bavdek)\par \par \uc2 USA-G20/YUAN|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|Z|UKI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100926e69q0009u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
