\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, peso down on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears; yuan up\b0\par\par\uc2 1,095 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 05:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Won, peso down 0.3 pct vs dlr; wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Spot yuan up 0.2 pct on U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 China FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  tension\par \par \uc2 * Baht down 0.2 pct on policy change caution\par \par \uc2 By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the Philippines peso fell against the dollar on Thursday as caution grew over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to curb strength in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But China's yuan rose as the People's Bank of China's (PBOC) set a stronger reference rate for a sixth straight day, even as U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner sharpened his criticism of Beijing's exchange rate policy.\par \par \uc2 "China's move today (on a higher yuan mid-point) seems to ease political tensions with the U.S. I don't think Beijing wants a strong yuan as other Asian countries don't allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise fast," said Kim Jae-eun, an economist at \uc2 Hyundai Securities\uc2  in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 China's Foreign Ministry said pressure would not solve the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue and could even have the opposite effect, pushing against a tide of criticism from Washington that the yuan is still sharply undervalued. [ID:nBJB003948]\par \par \uc2 There was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after it unleashed waves of yen selling <JPY=> on Wednesday to curb yen strength and help shore up its fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The yen rebounded about 0.5 percent against the dollar, despite expectations that Tokyo would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again soon. YUAN\par \par \uc2 The yuan <CNY=CFXS> rose against the dollar, scoring its fastest rise of 0.9 percent in six trading days since January 2008, guided by the People's Bank of China's (PBOC) strong reference rates.\par \par \uc2 Traders said Beijing was letting the yuan stage a "mini-revaluation" as the dollar's performance in global markets had been ignored, creating speculative opportunities for yuan appreciation among near-term offshore dollar/yuan forwards <CNYNDFOR=> up to three months.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set another record high mid-point for the yuan on Thursday even after the dollar <.DXY> rose 0.5 percent on Wednesday, a sign that the yuan's appreciation was being delinked from dollar movements for the time being.\par \par \uc2 Spot yuan <CNY=CFXS> was trading at 6.7272 against the dollar, up 0.22 percent from Wednesday's close of 6.7422, after touching an intraday high of 6.7250.\par \par \uc2 Short-dated dollar/yuan NDFs hovered near three-month lows, buoyed by the PBOC's mid-points, but the impact of the stronger fixing was fading beyond the short tenors, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "The market is thin and and people are reluctant to push lower at these levels as they are not clear about the near-term trend," says a trader at a brokerage house.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> fell against the dollar as importers buy dollars for settlements before the Chuseok holidays and investors added dollar positions amid heightened caution over further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by South Korean authorities.\par \par \uc2 The won also came under pressure from expected offers linked to \uc2 Hyundai Heavy Industries\uc2  purchase of a controlling stake in a local refiner from Abu Dhabi-based International Petroleum (IPIC).\par \par \uc2 Local dealers suspect IPIC has started to sell the won.\par \par \uc2 The won ended domestic trade down 0.30 percent at 1,164.5 per dollar from its previous domestic close <KRW=KFTC> of 1,160.9.\par \par \uc2 "Importers' deals are quite strong before the holidays and we will see more dollar demand (from IPIC). Given those dollar bids, it is difficult to try to break through 1,160," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \par \uc2 Seoul shares closed down 0.66 percent, but foreign investors remained net stock buyers purchasing a net 194.8 billion won worth of stocks on the main exchange.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 Thai baht <THB=> lost a quarter percent against the dollar as cautious investors remained wary of what \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  might do on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policy and despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assurance of no policy changes on Wednesday [ID:nSGE68E0AT].\par \par \uc2 "The market still chooses to be on guard against any BOT measures despite the assurance. Most dollar/Asia pairs are relatively steady today except the baht, and the yuan's new stronger mid-point fixing does not help curb the baht's fall [ID:nECB000513]," a dealer at a major Thai bank said.\par \par \uc2 Dollar/baht was bid at 30.90 against 30.83 late on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 Philippine peso <PHP=> fell as investors remained wary of possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cover dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2 Dealers also consolidated after a volatile Wednesday session, following Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 Peso slid 0.25 percent to 44.37 per dollar from its previous close of 44.26.\par \par \uc2 "Market is cautious over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They were last spotted at sub 44.30. I also see some short covering following the Asia equity reversal," said a Manila-based dealer.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was ready to prevent sharp moves in the peso. [ID:nSGE68E06A] \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0620 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        85.33          85.73       +0.47\par  Sing dlr        1.3380         1.3388       +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr      31.758         31.798       +0.13\par  Korean won     1164.50        1160.90       -0.30\par  Baht             30.90          30.83       -0.23\par  Peso             44.37          44.26       -0.25\par  Rupiah         8984.00        8985.00       +0.01\par  Rupee            46.32          46.35       +0.06\par  Yuan            6.7272         6.7422       +0.22 (Malaysia's\par financial markets were closed on a holiday)\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        85.33          92.90       +8.87\par  Sing dlr        1.3380         1.4053       +5.03\par  Taiwan dlr      31.758         32.030       +0.86\par  Korean won     1164.50        1164.50        0.00\par  Baht             30.90          33.32       +7.83\par  Peso             44.37          46.20       +4.12\par  Rupiah         8984.00        9420.00       +4.85\par  Rupee            46.32          46.54       +0.47\par  Ringgit         3.1160         3.4220       +9.82\par  Yuan            6.7272         6.8270       +1.48\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Vithoon Amorn in BANGKOK, Clement Tan in SINGAPORE, Saikat Chatterjee in HONG KONG, and Lu Jianxin in SHANGHAI) (Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28