\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 16\b0\par\par\uc2 1,739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 09:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =4TH UPDATE: BOJ LEAVES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CASH IN MARKET; JGBS RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan pumped liquidity into the banking system Thursday, in a sign it is trying to help the government weaken the yen by leaving cash from Wednesday's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the money market. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  YUAN HITS NEW HIGH AHEAD OF GEITHNER TESTIMONY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan hit another high against the U.S. dollar Thursday, despite the dollar's sharp rebound in international markets overnight, ahead of U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner's testimony at a Congressional hearing on China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: RBNZ HOLDS STEADY; MARKET PUSHES BACK HIKE FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand held interest rates steady Thursday and issued a surprisingly dovish policy statement, leading market players to push back their expectations for future rate hikes. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RBA'S LOWE SAYS ECONOMY MORE EXPOSED THAN EVER TO CHINA SWINGS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economy is more exposed than ever to the vagaries of Chinese economic growth, and little can be done to guard against uncertainties, Phil Lowe, Assistant Governor at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0530 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA PRIMARY ARTICLES WPI UP 0.2% IN WEEK TO SEPT 4 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale price index for primary articles rose 0.2% to 178.4 in the week to Sept. 4 from a provisional 178.0 the previous week, according to data issued Thursday by the Ministry of Commerce and Industry. (published 0625 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA BUSINESS CONFIDENCE SLUMPS IN 3Q - WESTPAC-ACCI SURVEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business confidence fell in the third quarter of 2010 compared with the previous quarter, a private sector survey showed Thursday. (published 0123 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA CONSUMER INFLATION EXPECTATIONS 3.1% IN SEPTEMBER VS 2.8% IN AUGUST-MI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian consumer inflationary expectations rose slightly in September after five straight months of declines, according to an industry survey published Thursday. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA EXPECTS KRW175 TLN TAX REVENUE 2010, KRW187.8 TLN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea raised its tax revenue forecast for this year as the domestic economy's recovery has boosted consumption and hence tax collection, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Thursday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : STRONG BAHT A FACTOR AT NEXT RATE MEETING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday the strong baht will be a factor at the Monetary Policy Committee's next policy rate meeting in October, raising the prospect that it may hold rates steady. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAILAND KEEPS 2010 EXPORT GROWTH TARGET BUT FLAGS STRONG BAHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's full-year export growth target remains intact at 20%, despite the baht's sharp rise against the U.S. dollar, Commerce Ministry Permanent Secretary Yanyong Phuangrach said Thursday. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI AUGUST INDUSTRIAL SENTIMENT TURNS DOWN ON BAHT WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's industrial sentiment index turned lower in August, after rising for two straight months, as corporate executives became worried about the baht's strength, rising interest rates, and the likely economic slowdown in the second half. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW ZEALAND MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY FLAT IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's manufacturing activity was flat in August after a steady expansion in the first half of the year, data released Thursday showed. (published 2306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA ECON PLANNER: CAN 'ABSOLUTELY' MEET 3% CPI TARGET THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic planning agency said late Wednesday the country can "absolutely" meet it target of around a 3% rise in the consumer price index this year, despite the CPI rising 3.5% from a year earlier in August. (published 0046 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN REGULATOR: BANKS' CAPITAL POSITION STRENGTHENED IN PAST 2 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The capital position of Taiwan's domestic banks strengthened over the past two years and the lenders should be able to withstand a crisis similar to 2008's global financial crisis, the island's banking regulator said Wednesday. (published 0112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CIC EXECUTIVE: INVESTMENT RETURNS TO STAY LOW IN MATURE FIXED-INCOME MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging markets are rising in importance as returns in mature fixed-income markets such as the U.S. and Europe are likely to stay low for five to 10 years, an executive with China's sovereign-wealth fund said Thursday. (published 0117 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA GOVERNMENT A$1.25B SEP 2030 INDEXED BONDS PRICE AT 2.66% REAL YIELD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian government said Thursday it has sold A$1.25 billion in 2.5% Sept. 20, 2030 Treasury-indexed bonds to the public. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: KIWI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SHOULD EMBRACE THE CHINA EFFECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand's forecasting pendulum has swung too far, too fast into gloomy territory. Demand from East Asia will ultimately steer New Zealand clear of its current malaise. (published 0512 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NINGBO PORT RAISES CNY7.4 BLN FROM SHANGHAI IPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ningbo Port Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a major port operator in eastern China, raised CNY7.4 billion from a smaller than planned Shanghai initial public offering, which would provide slightly more than half the funds for its planned port expansion and machine purchases. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =KINGFISHER AIRLINES GDR ISSUE ON HOLD UNTIL DEBT REVAMP PLAN FINALIZED -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kingfisher Airlines Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has put on hold its plan to raise about $200 million through an issue of global depositary receipts until it gets an approval from banks to restructure its debt, a person with direct knowledge of the matter said recently. (published 0533 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ALIBABA: MADE OFFER TO BUY BACK PART OF YAHOO'S STAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Internet giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  offered to buy back part of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yahoo Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s 39% stake in Alibaba, but \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yahoo\f28 \uc2 \f2  rejected the offer, Alibaba spokesman John Spelich said in a statement Thursday. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LOTTE CHILSUNG\f28 \uc2 \f2  BUYS 34.4% STAKE IN PEPSI COLA PRODUCTS PHILIPPINES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lotte Chilsung Beverage Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it has acquired a controlling 34.4% stake in Pepsi Cola Products Philippines for KRW118.4 billion to strengthen its presence in the overseas beverage market. (published 0222 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INTAS PHARMACEUTICALS TO SUPPLY GENERIC DRUGS TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 ASTRAZENECA\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intas Pharmaceuticals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has signed an agreement to license and provide generic drugs to \f28 \uc2 \f2 AstraZeneca PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  for sale in emerging markets, highlighting the trend of pharma majors looking at low-cost supplies to offset the pressure due to products coming out of patents. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KB FINANCIAL: TO SET ASIDE PROVISIONS PROACTIVELY FOR REST OF YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 KB Financial Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Thursday said that it will remain proactive in setting aside loan-loss provisions for the rest of the year. (published 0649 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA HUADIAN SEEKS BUYER FOR 13.65% STAKE IN YANTAI BANK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Huadian Corp., one of China's five major power utilities, is looking to raise funds by selling its 13.65% stake in Yantai Bank Co., the company said in a document filed to the Shanghai United Assets and Equity Exchange. (published 0053 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SOUTHERN: PRIVATE PLACEMENT PLAN GAINS REGULATORY APPROVAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Southern Airlines Co. said Thursday the China Securities Regulatory Commission has approved its plan to issue up to 1.77 billion new shares through a private placement. (published 2349 GMT) of the indicative range. (published 0032 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO INVEST MORE THAN $400 MLN IN WATER TREATMENT BUSINESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's LG Electronics Co. said Thursday that it will invest more than $400 million in water treatment \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the next 10 years with the aim of generating $7 billion in annual revenue from the business by 2020. (published 0225 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TSMC: PRETAX PROFIT LIKELY TO RISE ABOUT 10% ANNUALLY IN FUTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's largest contract chip manufacturer by revenue, expects its pretax profit to rise about 10% annually in the future, Chairman Morris Chang said Thursday, without providing a specific time frame. (published 0307 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MYER HOLDINGS\f28 \uc2 \f2  FY NET PROFIT A$67.2M, FINAL DIVIDEND 11.5C \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian department store retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Myer Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that its full year net profit came in at A$67.2 million, weighed down by costs associated with its November initial public offer. (published 2341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALINTA ENERGY: RECEIVED ALL TRADE BIDS FOR COMPANY, ASSETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alinta Energy Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday that it has received all trade bids for its whole business and individual assets and will assess them over the coming week. (published 2302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA CONSORTIUM TO INVEST KRW200B IN ROSEMONT COPPER MINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A South Korean consortium composed of state-run \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Resources Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., or Kores, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 LG International Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has signed a deal to acquire a 20% stake in the Rosemont copper mine in Arizona for KRW200 billion for a stable supply of the raw material. (published 0444 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY DOWN;JAPAN EXPORTERS EXTEND GAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower though Japanese exporters continued to benefit from a weaker yen after Japanese authorities' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  PROPOSES POWER TARIFF HIKE IN 7 PROVINCES -CITI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-09-10 0704GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economic planner has recommended an increase in electricity prices in seven provinces, a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  analyst said Thursday, in a move likely to add to inflation in China and which shows the problems the nation faces in keeping its economy supplied with energy. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA 2010 COAL OUTPUT COULD BE 10%-20% BELOW TARGET IF RAIN PERSISTS -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's coal production could be 10%-20% below its target of 270 million metric tons for this year if rain persists, a government official said Thursday. (published 0307 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CNPC, ROSNEFT TO FINALIZE JV REFINERY SEPTEMBER -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and OAO Rosneft will likely finalize an agreement to build a joint refinery in northern China's Tianjin city later this month, a senior Chinese official said Wednesday. (published 0006 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: TIME RIGHT FOR INDIA TO RESUME WHEAT EXPORTS -INDUSTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The timing is right for India to resume wheat exports given the weakening of the rupee over the last few months, massive government inventories of the grain and a bountiful monsoon season, several trading executives said Thursday. (published 0241 GMT) [ 16-09-10 0704GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100916e69g000h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
