\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Equities Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES LOWER BEFORE JOBLESS CLAIMS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock futures trade lower ahead of several reports that will provide more clues about the outlook for businesses in the largest global economy. Traders are also awaiting congressional testimony by Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US REGULATORS TO TARGET 'WINDOW DRESSING' \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal regulators are set to propose new disclosure rules targeting "window dressing," a practice undertaken by some large banks to temporarily lower their debt levels before reporting finances to the public.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YUAN AT NEW HIGH BEFORE GEITHNER TESTIMONY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan rises to another high against the dollar, despite the dollar's sharp rebound in international markets overnight, ahead of U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner's testimony on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ LEAVES SOME \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS IN MARKET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will leave in the market essentially all the yen sold in the government's huge \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , suggesting it is willing to help the government weaken the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to shore up the deflationary economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PRIMARIES STOKE TURMOIL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A tumultuous primary season ends with Republicans fielding a slate of conservatives they say will ride a wave of voter enthusiasm and Democrats countering that the GOP has overplayed its hand with far-right candidates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US LAYS OUT EXPORT PLAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Plan aims to double exports by focusing largely on small businesses and developing countries, even as the administration steps up efforts to gain access to China and other markets. Growth in sales abroad is outpacing the level needed to reach that goal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US WON'T RETRY KEY ENRON FIGURE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Justice Department drops charges against a former \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . official days before a scheduled retrial involving the only criminal case brought against Wall Street figures in the alleged misdeeds at the onetime energy giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Enron Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par J.P. MORGAN WRESTLES WEB SNARL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan Chase & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . struggles to restore electronic access to its online banking service, marking the third consecutive day of Internet interruptions and public-relations problems for the nation's second-largest bank by assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ORACLE SEEN POSTING SALES, PROFIT GAINS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts expect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oracle\f28 \uc2 \f2  to report earnings excluding one-time items of 36c a share for the period ended in August and $7.3 billion in revenue, according to data from FactSet Research.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WHITE HOUSE SEES LIMITED JOB LOSS FROM MORATORIUM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Obama Administration says most oil employers haven't laid off high-skilled oil workers despite the six-month ban on offshore oil drilling. White House figures show unemployment claims in the main drilling areas has actually declined from April through August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IN CHINA, FOREIGN BANKS LAG IN PROFITS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the first time, many foreign banks in China are offering a peek at their financial performance there, and the picture isn't pretty, Dinny McMahon writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par  \par TAKING STOCK \par Look Close To Home For Emerging Exposure \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If you'd like a piece of all that tempting emerging action you can build up perfectly respectable exposure to it without ever leaving the comfort of your home index. The miners are only the most obvious examples.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MORNING BRIEFING \par Stocks Seen Lower, Lacking Impetus \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stock futures are pointing to a flat to slightly lower open in the aftermath of Wednesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of Japan. The market will be looking to the weekly jobless data and PPI out later for direction.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par   ============ U.S. MARKETS ACTION =========== \par DJIA              10572.73 from Wednesday \par NASDAQ            2301.32 from Wednesday \par S&P 500           1125.07 from Wednesday \par 10-year T-note    99 7/32 at 2.7121 yield \par NYMEX Crude       down $0.80 at $75.23/bbl \par Dollar/Euro       up 0.0074 at 1.3081 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-16-10 0800ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5030 55101   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020100916e69g0003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
